chapter.atmticfq.theearlygame.name=The Early Game
chapter.atmticfq.theearlygame.desc=We always have to start somewhere, right?
quest.atmticfq.welcome.name=Welcome
quest.atmticfq.welcome.desc=Welcome to All The Mods That I Could Find.\n\nThis modpack contain all the mods that i could find and is divided in 1 major quest line and 6 secondary themed quest lines.\n\n-The Early Game: contain everything you need to start the modpack.\n- Stardew Farming: Contain quests about food, farming and fishing.\n- Computer Craft: Will guide you through the Computer Craft mod and it's major items\n- Storage: Has everything you need to store your items\n- Terrapon: Is what you need to be invincible. It contain alloys, tools and armors. Prepare to grind.\n\nPress the button to start the quest line. Have fun !
quest.atmticfq.gatherwood.name=Gather Wood
quest.atmticfq.gatherwood.desc=Start your adventure like any others. Mine 8 logs.
quest.atmticfq.workbench.name=Workbench
quest.atmticfq.workbench.desc=Craft your first workbench
quest.atmticfq.portable_workbench.name=Portable Workbench
quest.atmticfq.portable_workbench.desc=The same, except it's in your inventory.
quest.atmticfq.woodentools.name=Wooden Tools
quest.atmticfq.woodentools.desc=Craft your first wooden tools, you'll keep them for a bit longer than you'd want to.
quest.atmticfq.storage.name=Storage
quest.atmticfq.storage.desc=Craft a chest to store your first items.\n\nThis is the beginning of the Storage Quest line.
quest.atmticfq.bonetools.name=Bone Tools
quest.atmticfq.bonetools.desc=You'll need to wait the night to make your first Stone Pickaxe. Kill a skeleton and get two bones to make one.
quest.atmticfq.furnace.name=Burn your stuff
quest.atmticfq.furnace.desc=Craft a stone furnace to smelt your ores, you can use wood or charcoal to smelt things.
quest.atmticfq.ironfurnace.name=Iron Furnace
quest.atmticfq.ironfurnace.desc=Upgrade your furnace using 8 iron ingots to spare you time when smelting your ores.
quest.atmticfq.goldfurnace.name=Gold Furnace
quest.atmticfq.goldfurnace.desc=This upgrade will cost you a lot of gold but it's worth trust me.
quest.atmticfq.diamondfurnace.name=Fast Furnace
quest.atmticfq.diamondfurnace.desc=This is the fastest furnace you can have
quest.atmticfq.steelfurnace.name=Efficient Furnace
quest.atmticfq.steelfurnace.desc=This is the most efficient furnace you can have, but it will be slower to smelt ores.
quest.atmticfq.iron.name=Iron Ingot
quest.atmticfq.iron.desc=You will need a lot of this thing
quest.atmticfq.gold.name=Gold Ingot
quest.atmticfq.gold.desc=This is pretty rare and not that usefull by itself, but it's an ore used by many mods as an intermediary step toward upgraded items.
quest.atmticfq.lead.name=Lead Ingot
quest.atmticfq.lead.desc=A really useful ore that can duplicate dyes and bone meal.
quest.atmticfq.silver.name=Silver Ingot
quest.atmticfq.silver.desc=Used to craft iron things but way more efficient.
quest.atmticfq.diamond.name=Your first diamonds
quest.atmticfq.diamond.desc=A necessary step to become the best miner.
quest.atmticfq.diamondtool.name=Diamond Pick
quest.atmticfq.diamondtool.desc=You can now mine everything on earth.
quest.atmticfq.diamondtool2.name=Diamond Pick x9
quest.atmticfq.diamondtool2.desc=You can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.\nYou can now mine everything on earth.
quest.atmticfq.gotonether.name=Vacations in hell
quest.atmticfq.gotonether.desc=You'll need to mine some obsidian blocks and build a full portal frame to enter the Nether.
quest.atmticfq.glowstone.name=Glowing stone
quest.atmticfq.glowstone.desc=Oooh Shiny
quest.atmticfq.nethercoal.name=Nether Coal
quest.atmticfq.nethercoal.desc=Burn at higher temperatures. It allow you to craft a different kind of furnace and make steel ingots.
quest.atmticfq.steelingot.name=Steel Ingot
quest.atmticfq.steelingot.desc=Steel can be decrafted, so the best craft to make steel is to use iron blocks for now. Later, you'll be able to combine iron and Nether coal dust in an alloy smelter for 3 times less.
quest.atmticfq.signalindustries.name=The beginning of something greater
quest.atmticfq.signalindustries.desc=Your first Machine Core... and you'll make a lot of them.\n\nThis is the beginning of the Prototype-tier Quest Line.
quest.atmticfq.terrapon.name=Weaponry of the gods
quest.atmticfq.terrapon.desc=The Orb of Rogmal is the main component of every alloy you'll craft in this mod.\n\nThis is the beginning of the Terrapon Quest line.

chapter.atmticfq.storage.name=Storage
chapter.atmticfq.storage.desc=Everything you need to always have your inventory as clean as possible.
quest.atmticfq.cupboard.name=Vertical Chests
quest.atmticfq.cupboard.desc=Cupboards, just like chests can be combined in a "double" version but unlike chest they can only combine vertically. Put one cupboard on top of an other and you'll get a double cupboard with the same inventory space as a double chest.
quest.atmticfq.basicbackpack.name=Signal Industries Backpack
quest.atmticfq.basicbackpack.desc=Can store and entire chest of items and has 2 fluit slots of 2000. It is unable to store signaling energy.
quest.atmticfq.reinforcedbackpack.name=Reinforced Signal Industries Backpack
quest.atmticfq.reinforcedbackpack.desc=Can store and entire double chest of items and has 4 fluit slots of 4000. It is unable to store signaling energy.
quest.atmticfq.leatherbackpack.name=Cheapest Backpack
quest.atmticfq.leatherbackpack.desc=The most early game backpack, contain only 9 item slots but can be upgraded.
quest.atmticfq.ironbackpack.name=Backpack but grey
quest.atmticfq.ironbackpack.desc=An upgraded version of the leather backpack, contain 15 item slots and can be upgraded.
quest.atmticfq.goldbackpack.name=Backpack but piss
quest.atmticfq.goldbackpack.desc=An upgraded version of the iron backpack, contain 21 item slots and can be upgraded.
quest.atmticfq.diamondbackpack.name=Backpack but the best
quest.atmticfq.diamondbackpack.desc=The best BetterWithBackpack backpack, contain 27 item slots but cannot be upgraded anymore.
quest.atmticfq.moonsteelbackpack.name=Backpack but ender chest
quest.atmticfq.moonsteelbackpack.desc=It's a portable ender chest, contain 18 item slots and share it's items across every Stardust Backpack.
quest.atmticfq.prototypestoragecontainer.name=Prototype Storage Container
quest.atmticfq.prototypestoragecontainer.desc=It can store a lot of a single type of item similar to Crates but can be automated using Item Pipes.
quest.atmticfq.basicstoragecontainer.name=Basic Storage Container
quest.atmticfq.basicstoragecontainer.desc=Store even more of a single item, 4x more than the prototype tier.
quest.atmticfq.reinforcedcompressedstoragecontainer.name=Reinforced Compressed Storage Container
quest.atmticfq.reinforcedcompressedstoragecontainer.desc=Store way too much of a single item, 16x more than the prototype tier.
quest.atmticfq.ironchest.name=Chest but big
quest.atmticfq.ironchest.desc=A single block version of a double chest that cannot link itself to it's surroundings, can be upgraded.
quest.atmticfq.goldchest.name=Chest but big++
quest.atmticfq.goldchest.desc=A single block version of a triple chest that cannot link itself to it's surroundings, can be upgraded.
quest.atmticfq.diamondchest.name=Chest but way bigger++
quest.atmticfq.diamondchest.desc=A single block version of a quadruple chest that cannot link itself to it's surroundings, Maximum space management.
quest.atmticfq.steelchest.name=Chest but way bigger++ but cheaper
quest.atmticfq.steelchest.desc=Is the same size as it's diamond counterpart but is way cheaper, still maximum space management but also maximum stingy.
quest.atmticfq.crate.name=Crates
quest.atmticfq.crate.desc=It can store 48x stacks of a single item type and is really good to store your early game Cobblestone stacks. Can be stacked to increase storage size.

chapter.atmticfq.computercraft.name=Computer Craft
chapter.atmticfq.computercraft.desc=Grab your computer and become a nerd with this quest line
quest.atmticfq.computer.name=Your first Computer
quest.atmticfq.computer.desc=Computer Craft is a pretty complex mod that allow to make your own programs and code complex interactive behaviors with the world.\n\nComputers programs are made in a language named Lua, you can learn it here: https://www.lua.org/start.html.\nIf you don't want or can't learn Lua no worries, every computers start with a set of basic commands and programs to make your experience easier. You can also download scripts on the internet using the pastebin command "> pastebin get <url> <filename>".\n\nBasic behaviours will be explained in each quest. More info here: https://web.archive.org/web/20250420182424/https://www.computercraft.info/wiki/Computer
quest.atmticfq.pocketcomputer.name=Portable Computer
quest.atmticfq.pocketcomputer.desc=The same thing as a computer but can not interact with the world.
quest.atmticfq.wiredmodem.name=Local Area Network
quest.atmticfq.wiredmodem.desc=This block allow you to connect computers with each others using Networking Cables. You can interact with all connected computers. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/modem.html
quest.atmticfq.networkingcable.name=Networking Cables
quest.atmticfq.networkingcable.desc=By connecting two Wired Modem with Networking Cables you can make those two interact with each others. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/modem.html
quest.atmticfq.wirelessmodem.name=Wireless Connection
quest.atmticfq.wirelessmodem.desc=This block when placed on a computer will allow it to send and receive messages to and from other computers. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/modem.html
quest.atmticfq.floppydisk.name=Primitive Hard Drive
quest.atmticfq.floppydisk.desc=Floppy Disks are working like your typical hard drive, it can store files, folders and programs you can share with other players or store in a chest. More info here: https://web.archive.org/web/20190201194801/https://computercraft.info/wiki/Floppy_Disk
quest.atmticfq.diskdrive.name=Primitive USB Port
quest.atmticfq.diskdrive.desc=When placed on a computer the Disk Drive allow you to read Floppy Disks and read/run the files/programs stored inside.
quest.atmticfq.printer.name=Automatic TypeWriter
quest.atmticfq.printer.desc=When the Printer is placed on a computer, you can program your computer to print text on a paper with ink.
quest.atmticfq.monitor.name=Old 4/3 Screen
quest.atmticfq.monitor.desc=The Monitor display stuff in the world, you can make programs that draw text and images. Keep in mind that the screen is kinda low resolution and as such hard to use. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/monitor.html
quest.atmticfq.speaker.name=Turn up the volume!
quest.atmticfq.speaker.desc=Welcome to the world of Noises, with the Speaker you can now play sounds and many people made their own "Jukebox" programs with midi files have fun. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/speaker.html
quest.atmticfq.turtle.name=It doesn't look like a turtle.
quest.atmticfq.turtle.desc=Turtles are the most advanced types of computers, they can move in the world, place and break blocks as they please. Try using the program "excavate" stop it or it will dig down through the entire world lol. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/module/turtle.html
quest.atmticfq.advancedcomputer.name=Upgrade to Linux!
quest.atmticfq.advancedcomputer.desc=This upgraded version of the Computer allow the use of the mouse and can display colors and it's resolution is now 51/19 pixels! Amazing. More info here: https://computercraft.info/wiki/Advanced_Computer
quest.atmticfq.advancedpocketcomputer.name=Portable Linux
quest.atmticfq.advancedpocketcomputer.desc=Same thing as the old portable computer but better in the same way as the Advanced Computer. It has better resolution and can display colors.
quest.atmticfq.endermodem.name=5G Modem
quest.atmticfq.endermodem.desc=The same thing as the Wireless Modem but with infinite range and can send messages through dimensions.
quest.atmticfq.advancedmonitor.name=4K Screen
quest.atmticfq.advancedmonitor.desc=The best Monitor available, better resolution can display colors and has mouse support. You can ake menus to control the computer from the screen. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/peripheral/monitor.html
quest.atmticfq.advancedturtle.name=A really powerful turtle
quest.atmticfq.advancedturtle.desc=Same thing as the base turtle, with more features. More info here: https://tweaked.cc/module/turtle.html

chapter.atmticfq.stardewfarming.name=Stardew Farming
chapter.atmticfq.stardewfarming.desc=Farm everything everywhere, transform your dirt into farmlands and catch legendary fishes.
quest.atmticfq.fishingrod.name=3 Sticks and 2 Strings
quest.atmticfq.fishingrod.desc=Stardew Farming modified the fishing mechanic, you now have 4 different types of fish you can catch. Salmon, Snapper and Bass as well as 4 different Legendary fishes that will require you to fish in certain places at specific moments of the day.
quest.atmticfq.baitcan.name=Baited
quest.atmticfq.baitcan.desc=Worms can be used as baits but instead of keeping multiple stacks in your inventory, store them in a Bait Can.
quest.atmticfq.rawsnapper.name=Raw Snapper
quest.atmticfq.rawsnapper.desc=Can only be fished in summer.
quest.atmticfq.rawbass.name=Raw Bass
quest.atmticfq.rawbass.desc=Can only be fished in spring.
quest.atmticfq.rawsalmon.name=Raw Salmon
quest.atmticfq.rawsalmon.desc=Can only be fished in winter.
quest.atmticfq.rawfish.name=Raw Fish
quest.atmticfq.rawfish.desc=Can only be fished in autumn.
quest.atmticfq.cookedsnapper.name=Cooked Snapper
quest.atmticfq.cookedsnapper.desc=
quest.atmticfq.cookedbass.name=Cooked Bass
quest.atmticfq.cookedbass.desc=
quest.atmticfq.cookedsalmon.name=Cooked Salmon
quest.atmticfq.cookedsalmon.desc=
quest.atmticfq.cookedfish.name=Cooked Fish
quest.atmticfq.cookedfish.desc=
quest.atmticfq.legendary1.name=Lava Eel
quest.atmticfq.legendary1.desc=You have 1/15 chance of catching a Lava Eel when fishing in a lava lake.
quest.atmticfq.legendary2.name=Swordfish
quest.atmticfq.legendary2.desc=You have 1/15 chance of catching a Swordfish when the weather is stormy.
quest.atmticfq.legendary3.name=Ghostfish
quest.atmticfq.legendary3.desc=You have 1/15 chance of catching a Ghostfish when the weather is foggy and it's night time.
quest.atmticfq.legendary4.name=Stonefish
quest.atmticfq.legendary4.desc=You have 1/15 chance of catching a Stonefish when fishing in a deep cave starting from Y=32.
quest.atmticfq.pinkrecord.name=The legendary Pink Record
quest.atmticfq.pinkrecord.desc=Combine all you legendary fishes into the best music disk of all time.
quest.atmticfq.wateringcan.name=Watering Can
quest.atmticfq.wateringcan.desc=The Watering Can can interacts with a bunch of blocks and either puts stuff out of hydrates them, Spong to Wet Sponge, Farmland to Wet Farmland.
